77824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065283 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b2792086-a352-5ca3-b086-f381a58864aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065283 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186065417 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065284 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065284 #edb/ref 1061 77825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065284 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "503ce197-02ae-5ae2-897a-80af7de15a2a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065284 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064358 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065285 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065285 #edb/ref 1061 77828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065285 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b129822d-f637-5611-9cad-e2f8b6aefca4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065285 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186065418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065286 #edb/ref 1061 77829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065286 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8ddc832d-59f9-5fa2-85e2-002f7b9c4ccc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065286 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064359 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065416 #edb/ref 1064 "Dividing with negative numbers follows similar rules as multiplying with negative numbers.\n\nFirst of all, a negative number divided by a positive number gives a negative number. We can picture this rule as\n\n$$\n(-)\\div(+) = (-)\n$$\n\nFor example, let's use this rule to find the value of $(-6) \\div 2$.\n\nHere, since we are dividing a negative number $\\color{red}(-6)$ by a positive number ${\\color{blue}(2)}$, the result is going to be negative:\n$3$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $6$ by $2$ *without* any signs:\n\n$$\n6 \\div 2 = 3\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-6)} \\div {\\color{blue}2} = {\\color{red} -3}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065416 #edb/ref 1065 8108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065416 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b92ac2e4-b983-5fd5-bc18-7dfb821497f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065416 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065417 #edb/ref 1064 "A positive number divided by a negative number is also a negative number. We can picture this rule as\n\n$$\n(+)\\div(-) = (-)\n$$\n\nFor instance, to find $8\\div (-2)$, we have to divide a positive number $\\color{blue}(8)$ by a negative one ${\\color{red}(-2)}$. So the result will be negative:\n$10$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $8$ by $2$ without any signs:\n\n$$\n8 \\div 2 = 4\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}8} \\div {\\color{red}(-2)} = {\\color{red}-4}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065417 #edb/ref 1065 8109 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065417 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "67beb927-7da4-5576-8982-1a823c878691" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065417 #edb/ref 1067 "The Quotient of a Positive and a Negative is a Negative" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065418 #edb/ref 1064 "Finally, the third rule is that a negative number divided by a negative number is a positive number:\n\n$$\n(-)\\div(-) = (+)\n$$\n\nTo demonstrate, let's find $-12 \\div (-3)$. We have to divide a negative number $\\color{red}(-12)$ by another negative number ${\\color{red}(-3)}$. So the result will be positive:\n$4$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $12$ by $3$ without any signs:\n\n$$\n12 \\div 3 = 4\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-12)} \\div {\\color{red}(-3)} = {\\color{blue}4}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065418 #edb/ref 1065 8111 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065418 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b1d3d95e-7953-5c5b-b97b-d4eb85e1f80d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065418 #edb/ref 1067 "The Quotient of a Negative and a Negative is a Positive" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
